# 1. Project Overview

Meridian is a geospatial intelligence platform that allows users to discover nearby places, search using spatial filters, view locations on an interactive map, and access review information.

The project uses multiple database technologies:

| Technology | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| PostgreSQL 16 | Relational data storage |
| PostGIS 3.7 | Geographic data and spatial queries |
| pgvector 0.8.7 | Vector embeddings and semantic search |
| MongoDB 8.0 | GPS trajectory storage and analytics |
| Next.js 16 | Frontend and API routes |
| React Leaflet 5 | Interactive map |
| Docker Compose | Database infrastructure |

The application is built to demonstrate advanced DBMS concepts, including spatial indexing, document databases, vector similarity search, transactions, triggers, full-text search and aggregation.

